{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"pwd && sed -n '1,240p' __issue_context__.json && git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl\n{\n  \"body\": \"The textual and logical definition for this term limits IELs to \\\"intestinal epithelium\\\" only, but IELs are found in multiple epithelial tissues - Gastrointestinal tract, Reproductive tract, oral cavity etc... \\n\\n1) Broaden the definition of \\\"intraepithelial lymphocyte\\\"\\n2) Add a specific subclass \\\"intestinal intraepithelial lymphocyte\\\"\\n\\n**Improved textual definition**\\nA tissue-resident lymphocyte located within the epithelial layer of mucosal tissues, particularly within the gastrointestinal, respiratory, and reproductive tracts. Characterised by permanent residency, this cell typically expresses CD103 (ntegrin alpha-E), which binds to E-cadherin on epithelial cells, enabling epithelial retention in both mice and humans. Phenotypically, IEL displays an activated, antigen-experienced state characterised by the constitutive expression of cytotoxic molecules (granzyme B, perforin) and innate-like receptors (such as NKG2D), enabling rapid, localised surveillance and immediate response to epithelial stress.\\n\\n**Add these references (DO NOT replace existing ones)**\\n\\nPMID: [29674648](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29674648/)\\nWIKIPEDIA:Intraepithelial lymphocyte\\n\\n**Logical definition**\\n'mature T cell'\\n and ('located in' some 'epithelium')\\n and ('capable of' some 'mucosal immune response')\\n\\n--- \\n\\n**intestinal intraepithelial lymphocyte**\\n\\n**textual definition**\\nA T cell that is located in the intestinal epithelium and is capable of a mucosal immune response.\\n\\nPMID: [29674648](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29674648/)\\nWIKIPEDIA:Intraepithelial lymphocyte\\n\\n**logical definition**\\n\\nEquivilantTo\\n'mature T cell'\\n and ('located in' some 'intestinal epithelium')\\n and ('capable of' some 'mucosal immune response')\\n\\n**ORCID**\\nhttps://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277\\n\\n\",\n  \"comments\": [],\n  \"title\": \"Revise intraepithelial lymphocyte and subclasses\",\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3346\"\n}\n D .github/copilot-instructions.md\n?? AGENTS.md\n?? __agent_config__/\n?? __agent_prompt__.md\n?? __issue_context__.json\n?? __pr_result__/\n?? obo-scripts/\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
